 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t a single objectively “best” manager for every rental home, but **Homestretch Property Management** is a reasonable first company to interview. Its site features owner testimonials praising communication and help with leasing, accounting, and tenant care. That’s a useful lead, not independent proof of performance.\n\nI’d also get a proposal from **Deca Property Management** and compare them on the same points:\n\n- Total fees, including leasing, renewals, maintenance coordination, and any vacancy or setup charges  \n- How they screen tenants and handle late rent or evictions  \n- Typical time to lease a home like yours in its neighborhood  \n- Maintenance approval limits and whether they mark up vendor invoices  \n- Sample owner statements and the termination clause  \n\nAsk for recent owner references and verify that the company and its agents are properly licensed in Missouri. The best choice will depend on your home’s location, condition, and how hands-on you want to be.",
